Kurokesu libcamera packaging notes
==================================

This package is a Kurokesu fork of Raspberry Pi's libcamera packaging.
The recipe lives on a single DEP-14 `debian/latest` branch and reuses
RPi's recipe verbatim where possible. Deviations are kept minimal,
profile-driven, and tracked here so they can be retired when no longer
needed.

Identity adaptations
--------------------

These define Kurokesu's fork:

  * Version scheme: `0.7.1+rpt<date>+krks<N>-<M>`. The `+krks<N>`
    counter resets on each RPi resync; `-<M>` is the Debian packaging
    revision.
  * `Maintainer`, `Uploaders`, `Vcs-*`, `watch`, `gbp.conf` repointed
    to github.com/Kurokesu/libcamera.

Build-environment deviations (retirable)
----------------------------------------

pkg.libcamera.nonn profile
  Why:         bookworm lacks libtensorflow-lite-dev (NN-AWB).
  Retire when: bookworm dropped, or libtensorflow-lite-dev reaches the
               RPi bookworm archive.

noqt wired through d/rules
  Why:         RPi declared pkg.libcamera.noqt in debian/control
               (guarding qt6-base-dev) but debian/rules never read the
               profile, so requesting it dropped the build-dep yet
               still passed -Dqcam=enabled and failed dep-resolution.
  Retire when: RPi merges the same fix to pios/trixie.

python3-packaging <!nocheck>
  Why:         test/v4l2_compat/v4l2_compat_test.py imports
               `from packaging import version`; that module is not
               in bookworm's build chroot, so the test errored out
               instead of reaching its normal "no devices" skip.
  Retire when: RPi adds the build-dep upstream, or bookworm dropped.

Seed
----

  * Source: github.com/raspberrypi/libcamera, branch `pios/trixie`.
  * Last seed: 896780d3 (libcamera 0.7.1+rpt20260429-1).
  * Reseed procedure: replace `debian/` wholesale with the new seed's
    contents, reapply this file's deviations, prepend a new changelog
    entry, build on both supported suites.

Editing rule
------------

Any Kurokesu-specific change to `debian/control` or `debian/rules`
(adding a profile, adding/removing a build-dep, retiring a deviation)
must update the deviations section above in the same commit.
